{"chunk_id": "d70d2e73d5af", "text": "Lakshmana rebukes Rama for speaking despairingly and urges him to remember his vow: Ravana must die before the day ends so that Sita can be rescued. Stirred by these words, Rama resumes the battle. Ravana charges in his chariot while Rama initially fights on foot, prompting the gods to judge the combat unfair. Indra sends his divine charioteer Matali with a celestial chariot, weapons, and horses for Rama. Mounted now, Rama and Ravana engage in a terrifying duel using supernatural weapons. Ravana unleashes serpent-arrows that become venomous snakes, but Rama counters with the Garuda weapon, transforming arrows into eagle-like serpent-slayers. Ravana retaliates fiercely, wounding Rama and striking Indra\u2019s chariot. Cosmic omens shake the universe as their rage escalates, and the watching gods and demons take sides. Finally Ravana raises a dreadful, world-ending lance and challenges Rama directly.\nRama and Ravana resume their fierce duel; Indra sends his chariot to aid Rama as divine weapons clash and Ravana unleashes a terrifying spear.\nThemes: epic duel, divine intervention, celestial weapons, cosmic omens, heroic resolve", "vector": [-0.000641460414044559, -0.025818364694714546, -0.010703224688768387, 0.014595306478440762, -0.016194792464375496, 0.004645172972232103, -0.03937400504946709, -0.020420100539922714, -0.031056679785251617, -0.016048172488808632, 0.024018943309783936, 0.027377862483263016, 0.019393764436244965, 0.00019212572078686208, 0.006541229784488678, 0.011802871711552143, 0.04406582936644554, -0.007151033729314804, 0.026324868202209473, -0.002747449791058898, -0.008877145126461983, -0.019433751702308655, -0.003505539381876588, 0.02649814635515213, -0.026804713532328606, 0.0016744615277275443, 0.018607350066304207, -0.03361585736274719, 0.017514368519186974, -0.017621001228690147, -0.018540704622864723, -0.024872001260519028, 0.000669368077069521, -0.011722897179424763, -0.02019350603222847, -0.0004181988479